title AMUS7 — Constel gossip: one frame reaches the whole constellation at once
prompt Keaton set the recursion loop on the 1024-round itinerary and six-season double-seat: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, make progress before checking in, send often as its own signed round, stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think AMUS6 (switchboard) landed and sent this turn — a whole local constellation routes point-to-point by name. The next AMUS rung, the socket, crosses the Comlink seam and is a custody gate. Lindy-first crux-first among the agent-doable: the switchboard routes to ONE named pier, yet the shape a real network leans on for a shared fact (a member joining, a name claimed, a block proposed) is ONE-TO-MANY. Broadcast is the primitive every gossip and flood protocol stands on, and the honest bridge from the point-to-point AMUS ladder toward the constel consensus track already sketched (pond/apps/constel_consensus*.rye, a separate silo).
think The one genuinely new concern: fan a single frame out to the whole constellation at once. broadcast(sb, from, frame) refuses NoSuchPier if the announcer is not a member (BEFORE any mailbox is touched, so a stranger never causes a partial fan-out), then walks the roster and delivers the frame to each OTHER member's mailbox — never the announcer's own — returning the count reached (size-1 on a clean fan-out). Each recipient reads its own copy with the ordinary switchboard.receive, so a broadcast is MANY honest deliveries, never a shortcut around the border: the two AMUS3 gates (Sha256 + naming-law border) run per recipient at wire.deframe_*.
think One file, one function over AMUS6 — no new value model, no new bound beyond the switchboard's own max_piers mailboxes. The invariants carry the correctness: reached == n-1 on a clean fan-out, the announcer skipped at from_slot, the walk bounded by the roster count. Named gossip.rye (Comlink-tendency: clear, fun, names the direction — the consensus track it feeds).
obs Witness GREEN on the FIRST run (like AMUS6 — reusing proven values/bounds leaves nothing new to trip on). Five proofs: a broadcast in a sky of four lands one whole frame in each of the other three mailboxes (count three) and never the announcer's own; each recipient reads its own copy byte-for-byte and independently (one reading does not consume another's); a broadcast of two degenerates cleanly to a single delivery; a stranger's announce refuses NoSuchPier before any mailbox is touched (every member still empty afterward — no partial fan-out); and a broadcast frame carrying a smuggled vowel is delivered to every mailbox yet each recipient's deframe still refuses VowelPresent. Witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, width exit 0; prior AMUS rungs stay GREEN (additive).
obs Kept docs synced (docs-implementation-sync): constel/README.md gains the gossip rung, the run block lists amus_gossip_witness, Status and Kin weave include AMUS7, the road-on names gossip standing beneath the socket, and the stamp advanced to 050801. The socket remains the only rung that stops for Keaton's word.
loom witness=amus_gossip_witness blocks=5 constellation_piers=4 fan_out_reached=3 mailboxes=8 greeting_frame_bytes=64 wall_ms_note=selftest under a second after build
